NAME
       sestatus - show the SELinux status

SYNOPSIS
       sestatus [-b]

DESCRIPTION
       sestatus prints whether SELinux is enabled, the loaded policy
       (targeted on RHEL), the current mode (enforcing or permissive), the
       mode set in /etc/selinux/config (used at the next boot) and other
       details. When the two modes differ, the system was switched with
       setenforce and will go back to the config file's mode at reboot.

OPTIONS
       -b     Also list every boolean and whether it is on or off.

EXAMPLES
       Check the current and the boot-time mode:

           sestatus
           getenforce
           grep ^SELINUX= /etc/selinux/config

FILES
       /etc/selinux/config
              SELINUX=enforcing|permissive|disabled, the mode at boot.

SEE ALSO
       getenforce(8), setenforce(8), selinux(8), getsebool(8)
